# Hospital Staff Attrition Analysis

A Power BI dashboard analyzing employee attrition across a hospital system — tracking turnover, burnout, overtime, and resignation drivers by department and role to help HR and department heads identify retention risk before it becomes a resignation.

## 📊 Dashboard Preview

![Attrition Analysis Dashboard](Attrition%20.png)

## 🎯 Business Problem

Hospital departments were losing staff to attrition without a consolidated view of *why* — no single place showed turnover rate, replacement cost, burnout levels, and resignation drivers together. This dashboard consolidates HR and workforce data into one view so leadership can see which departments and roles are highest-risk, and what's actually driving exits.

## 📈 Key Metrics

- **Staff Turnover Rate (%)** — share of headcount lost to attrition
- **Total Exit Replacement Cost ($)** — cumulative cost of replacing departed staff
- **Average Burnout Index** — composite burnout score across active staff
- **Average Monthly Overtime Hours** — workload pressure indicator
- **High Overtime Alert** — gauge flagging staff exceeding a safe overtime threshold
- **Salary Payroll Lost to Attrition** — active vs. resigned vs. terminated payroll split
- **Primary Resignation Reasons** — Salary, Personal, Better Compensation, and other exit drivers
- **Resignations by Hospital Department** — Nephrology, Emergency, Radiology, Intensive Care, Neonatal, Operating Room, Cardiology, General Surgery
- **Staff Burnout & Tenure Matrix** — overtime hours and tenure trended by role
- **Overtime Hours vs. Burnout Index by Role** — correlation between workload and burnout

## 📁 Repository Contents

| File | Description |
